The component is switched strongly negative on the word "and" (the English
conjunction that joins clauses, items or names), and the token is the same
whether it is capitalised or not. It is also negative, but less so, on "or"
and on the conjunctions of other languages (und, и, et, ou, oder, 和, 或, ...),
and weakly on the ampersand symbols "&" and "&&". On every other token it is
near zero, which is why the program predicts 0 there.

Predicted activation per token (a negative number means "and"-like):
  "and" (any case, also "-and" / "_and")  -3.3
  "or"                                    -1.5
